── §76 · per-token values — the valued run, and the token that wraps whole
· room to spare — one ground per valued token, and none on the words between them
................................................................................ The parser tracks quotes with a boolean, so a nested quote flips it back.

· squeezed — a valued token that cannot fit moves down WHOLE, its ground unbroken across no line: \`atomsOf\` emits an atom per valued run
........................................ The parser tracks quotes with a boolean,
........................................ so a nested quote flips it back early.

── §26 · the trail and the mark at the head — two carriers, and what each survives
· streaming, hot edge — the head arrives above the accent, the design's overshoot (C09 I133), and the band cools over the last fourteen CELLS toward the run's own ink, and the mark sits one space past the head in accent
................................................................................ The parser tracks quotes with a single boolean, which is why ⋅

· settled — no band and no mark: nothing replaces the mark and nothing is left behind (R-BLK-188)
................................................................................ The parser tracks quotes with a single boolean, which is why

· streaming at 1-bit — the trail is gone and the mark is not: colour dies, shape does not, which is what makes them two carriers and not one fact twice
................................................................................ The parser tracks quotes with a single boolean, which is why ⋅

· the reservation, at the width where it shows — 48 columns, streaming: the mark's two cells come off the wrap, so \`boolean,\` moves down
................................................ The parser tracks quotes with a single
................................................ boolean, which is why ⋅

· and the same block settled at 48 — \`boolean,\` stays up, which is the two cells, and it is the whole of what \`measure\` has to agree with
................................................ The parser tracks quotes with a single boolean,
................................................ which is why

